{{#api.hasAsyncapi}}
## Event contracts

`src/main/asyncapi/asyncapi.yaml` declares the CloudEvents types this service sends and receives.
Payload records use JDK types and retain the version in their class names. `axiz generate event
<name-vN>` reads the declared payload. `axiz contract sync --type asyncapi` creates new records
and `.axiz-new` proposals without replacing existing implementations. Review and merge proposals,
then implement the subscribed handlers before consuming live messages. The generated typed
skeletons reject messages until their business action is implemented; their Spring AOT binding
metadata stays in `config`, outside the payload layer.

`axiz doctor` checks receive subscriptions and the snapshot. `axiz contract diff --type asyncapi
old.yaml new.yaml` rejects incompatible published types; optional fields can extend vN, while
other changes require a new type in parallel. CI compares the contract with an earlier immutable
Git revision even when the current snapshot was updated. Local lint checks structure; corporate
Spectral rules run in CI. Business meaning still requires human review.
{{/api.hasAsyncapi}}

